3 Companion: verifying parity against ‘package.el’
**************************************************

A sibling file, elpaca-build-augment-audit.el
(elpaca-build-augment-audit.el), downloads the latest tarball for each
package from GNU/NonGNU ELPA or MELPA and diffs it against the Elpaca
build dir, so you can confirm — per package or across the whole config —
that nothing a ‘package.el’ user would have is missing from your Elpaca
install.  See TEST.org (TEST.org) for the full writeup and the three
entry points (‘M-x elpaca-build-augment-audit’, ‘-audit-all’, and the
opt-in ‘elpaca-build-augment-audit-watch’ list).


