5.1 Metadata source: ‘elpaca-build-augment-sources’
===================================================

Where the ‘elpa-packages’ files come from.  Two presets are shipped:

   • ‘elpaca-build-augment--sources-emacsmirror’ (default) — the
     ‘emacsmirror’ GitHub mirrors of ‘elpa.git’ / ‘nongnu-elpa.git’.
     Backed by GitHub's CDN, fast and stable.
   • ‘elpaca-build-augment--sources-savannah’ — the upstream Savannah
     cgit endpoints.  Authoritative, but cgit is frequently overloaded
     and returns 502 error pages under traffic bursts.  Opt in if you
     specifically want first-source reads.

   You can also set the variable to an arbitrary alist to point at any
other host (a local mirror, a corporate proxy, etc.).  See the
‘defcustom’ docstring for the plist shape.

     ;; Opt into Savannah upstream instead of emacsmirror.
     (setopt elpaca-build-augment-sources
             elpaca-build-augment--sources-savannah)


