5.2 Metadata caching: ‘elpaca-build-augment-cache-metadata’
===========================================================

Boolean, default ‘t’.

   • ‘t’ — the fetched snapshots are persisted on disk under
     ‘<user-emacs-directory>/elpaca-build-augment-cache/’ and reused
     across Emacs sessions.  Call ‘M-x elpaca-build-augment-refresh’ to
     pull fresh copies.
   • ‘nil’ — no disk cache.  The snapshots are fetched once per Emacs
     session into an in-memory index and reused for every package
     install in that session; ‘M-x elpaca-build-augment-refresh’ forces
     a refetch within a session.

   Disk caching is recommended for normal use — the metadata changes
slowly and a stale copy only costs you a build step or two on a
newly-added field.  Choose ‘nil’ if you specifically want every Emacs
session to start from fresh upstream metadata.

     (setopt elpaca-build-augment-cache-metadata nil)


