5.6 Overriding on a per-package basis
=====================================

Nothing library-specific is needed.  The hook only ever returns
‘:build’, and only when the user hasn't already set it.  Everything else
— ‘:branch’, ‘:repo’, ‘:files’, ‘:ignored-files’ — can be adjusted
inline in the ‘(elpaca ...)’ / ‘(use-package ... :ensure (...))’ form;
Elpaca's recipe merging gives the user's declaration higher precedence
than the menu's.  To exempt a specific package from augmentation
entirely, just declare its own ‘:build’ yourself — the hook sees the
field is set and skips the package.

     ;; Change a repo field inline — hook doesn't touch :branch, so it stays.
     (use-package somepkg :ensure (:branch "release"))

     ;; Opt out of augmentation for one package by giving it an explicit :build.
     (use-package weirdpkg :ensure (:build nil))


